*.md
.clineignore
.git
resume/

# Internal only -- never ship these to the public site.
# design-candidates/ holds 11 rejected drafts. Until this line was added they
# deployed with the site and were publicly reachable at
# /design-candidates/<name>.html, and crawlable (robots.txt allows everything).
design-candidates/
docs/
scripts/
.superpowers/

# index.html loads exactly ONE thing from vendor/: fonts.css (and vendor/fonts/).
# Everything else in vendor/ exists only for the design candidates, and
# design-candidates/ is already excluded above -- so all of it was shipping
# publicly for no reason. Two problems with that, both fixed here:
#
#   1. LICENSE. vendor/mesh/brain-mni.bin is derived from aces/brainbrowser,
#      which is AGPL-3.0 (see vendor/mesh/README-LICENSE.md). It was being
#      served at /vendor/mesh/brain-mni.bin -- verified HTTP 200, 2,703,404
#      bytes, on 2026-08-05. Distributing an AGPL asset carries source-
#      provision obligations. It is not referenced by index.html at all.
#   2. WEIGHT. three.js + postprocessing + the HDR env map + the mesh is
#      several MB of public dead weight on a site whose whole argument is
#      that it loads fast.
#
# DO NOT use `vendor/*` + `!vendor/fonts/` here. That pattern is correct under
# git's matcher (verified) but Vercel did NOT honour the directory re-include:
# deployed 2026-08-05, /vendor/fonts/IBMPlexSans-400.woff2 came back 404 and the
# live site silently fell back to system fonts. Caught by post-deploy checks.
#
# Every exclusion is therefore listed EXPLICITLY, with no negation to get wrong.
# Keep in sync if anything new is vendored: the only things the live index.html
# loads from vendor/ are fonts.css and the seven woff2 files it references.
vendor/mesh/
vendor/hdr/
vendor/lines/
vendor/loaders/
vendor/objects/
vendor/shaders/
vendor/postprocessing/
vendor/postprocessing.module.js
vendor/three.core.min.js
vendor/three.module.min.js
vendor/RoomEnvironment.js
vendor/gsap.min.js
vendor/lenis.min.js
vendor/ScrollTrigger.min.js
